---
/**
 * What this is, and the confusion it exists to clear up.
 *
 * The one job: a reader — human or agent — arriving here should leave knowing
 * this shop sells a CERAMIC OBJECT. The measured failure that made these pages
 * worth writing was exactly that gap: asked what glizzy.store is, an agent went
 * and found an article about the slang word and answered from its own memory.
 *
 * Written plainer than the homepage on purpose. Everything a person reads on
 * the front page is deadpan, and that is right there; this page is where a
 * verifier checks whether the shop is real, and a joke it cannot detect is a
 * fact it will repeat. Facts only, in the site's register but not its jokes.
 *
 * Every claim comes off the product listing (ceramic, hand made, unique, US
 * clay, crafted and packed in Vinton VA, ~1.5 inches, not for kids) or the
 * "...What Now?" panel, plus the store's own shipping setting for the US-only
 * line. Nothing about production volume, sourcing beyond the clay, or who else
 * is involved, because none of that is stated anywhere.
 *
 * A draft of this page also said there is no wholesale and no custom ordering.
 * That was cut for the same reason it was cut from llms.txt an hour earlier:
 * plausible, stated nowhere, and a trust page is the worst place to guess.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteIcon from '../components/SiteIcon.astro';
import ProsePage from '../components/ProsePage.astro';
import { AUTHOR } from '../lib/productJsonLd';
import { buyHref } from '../lib/fetchShopifyProducts';

const shop = await buyHref();
const description =
  'Old Vinton Glizzys are small ceramic hot dogs, hand made in Vinton, Virginia. Not food, not the slang. A fired ceramic object about an inch and a half long.';
---

<Layout title="About — Glizzy Store" description={description} scripts={false}>
  <SiteIcon />
  <ProsePage heading="About">
    <p>
      Glizzy Store sells one thing: a small ceramic hot dog, roughly an inch and a half long. Each
      one is hand made, so each one is slightly different from the last. The clay is mined in the
      United States, and the crafting, firing and packing all happen in Vinton, Virginia.
    </p>

    <h2>It is a ceramic object</h2>
    <p>
      This is not food. It is fired
      ceramic: a keepsake built to outlast any meat-based frankfurter by a considerable margin. It
      is small enough to put in a pocket without anyone nearby being any the wiser.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>
      Not for kids. Not a food product, and nothing here is edible or should be treated as though
      it were. What is in the shop is what there is. Orders ship within the United States only.
      The store offers no international delivery.
    </p>

    <h2>Who makes it</h2>
    <p>
      Made and packed in Vinton, Virginia. This site is written by {AUTHOR.name}. The shop runs on
      Shopify, and checkout happens on <strong>shop.vinton.land</strong>. That is the same store
      under a different name, and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> has what it means for
      your details.
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      <a href={shop}>The glizzy itself</a> has the current price and whether it is in stock. The
      credits are in the <a href="/colophon/">colophon</a>, and
      <a href="/contact/">the contact page</a> reaches a person.
    </p>
  </ProsePage>
</Layout>
